export const CAMERA_SKILL_MARKDOWN = "---\nname: haik-camera\ndescription: Use the Haik camera MCP to inspect saved live or historical frames, collect persistent local screenshots and recordings, and perform user-requested PTZ surveys. Applies to camera observations, timed sampling, recording lookup, surrounding views, and camera connection errors.\n---\n\n# Haik camera MCP\n\nRead this once per connection. This server exposes camera selection, recording lookup/playback, direct decoded screenshots, persistent capture jobs, temporary stream URLs, bounded PTZ movement, and stopping. It does not analyze pictures or perform a complete panoramic scan itself. Follow the user's scope and the harness's permissions; these instructions do not grant access or authorize new actions.\n\n## Fast path\n\n- Discover this skill with `resources/read` at `haik://skills/haik-camera/SKILL.md`. Tools-only clients can call `camera_usage_guide` with `{}`. Both work before account login and do not contact cameras.\n- Before observation, check that this harness can access and view saved images returned by the local server. The server performs decoding and saving for the integrated capture tools; the receiving harness still needs image viewing and access to the returned paths or download URLs. Explain a missing access/viewing capability before starting dependent camera work.\n- Use `list_cameras` once to obtain real IDs. Reuse the selected ID in the current task; refresh after account changes, a missing camera, or stale/offline results. Do not guess IDs or silently switch devices. If several devices fit the request and no prior selection resolves it, clarify the target once.\n- `camera_connection_status` checks the account, not live picture availability. Use it for login/connection troubleshooting instead of before every frame or operation.\n- Use `camera_snapshot` for one current frame. For a timed observation, use `camera_capture_start` with `kind: \"frames\"`, normally `durationSeconds: 10`, `fps: 1`, `maxWidth: 1280`, and `quality: 2`. These tools acquire their own authorized source; do not call `get_live_stream` first. Follow the returned `job.id` with `capture_status`, inspect actual saved files, and use `capture_list` to resume work after a reconnect. A pending snapshot needs status for the same job, not another snapshot request.\n- Use `camera_capture_start` with `kind: \"video\"` when the user requests a saved local video. This creates an H.264 MP4 at 15 fps without audio. For image analysis, prefer frame capture or directly decode the saved MP4 at the requested sampling rate.\n- Use `get_live_stream` only when a separate direct decoder is needed. Reuse an already obtained, unexpired URL for the selected camera/quality, normally quality 2 (quality 1 for detail), within its approximately 300-second lifetime. Do not obtain one URL per frame. Keep signed URLs out of reports and shell arguments.\n- Save directly decoded frames, then inspect those files. Never read camera data using computer use, browser screenshots, or screenshots of a video player. For capture jobs, artifact access, and the optional direct-decoder helper, read [references/capture.md](references/capture.md), also available at `haik://skills/haik-camera/references/capture.md` or through `camera_usage_guide` with `{\"section\":\"capture\"}`.\n\n## Historical recordings\n\n- Use `camera_capabilities` when support is unknown; protocol capability does not prove there are recordings. Query `camera_recordings` with the selected camera, a Beijing date (`YYYY-MM-DD`), and `source: \"cloud\"` or `\"sd\"`. Follow the user's requested source and time; clarify only when the target cannot be inferred.\n- The current account token does not support the recording month calendar. If `camera_recording_dates` reports unavailable, query the selected date directly instead of retrying the calendar, manufacturing dates, or requesting another login. An empty recording list means no matching recording was returned; do not substitute live video as historical evidence.\n- Use a returned `recordId` with the same `date` and `source` for `camera_playback`, or for `camera_capture_start` with `mode: \"playback\"`. SD playback also accepts the advertised Beijing `startTime`/`endTime` format. Keep capture duration within the selected segment. Do not bypass encrypted or unavailable recordings.\n- Distinguish historical recording time in `sourceInfo` from the local capture task's approximate `capturedAt`. Label playback clearly and keep PTZ stationary during historical review unless the user separately requests live movement.\n\n## Observation contract\n\n- Save one frame per second unless the user explicitly requests another rate. Respect their duration; when omitted, take a bounded 10-second sample and state that duration. A 15-second sample means 15 frames at video-relative times 0 through 14 seconds. A request for a short sample does not start ongoing monitoring.\n- Preserve original frames and record frame count, relative timestamps, capture time, camera ID, and accessible artifact locations. Use returned paths, SHA256 values, and the downloadable JSON manifest to continue analysis later. `capturedAt` is approximate local task time plus decoded sample time, not a verified camera exposure time. Keep relative time, historical `sourceInfo`, and the camera's displayed wall clock separate. If a frame is upside down, inspect it first and preserve the raw file when making an upright analysis copy.\n- Inspect actual saved frames before describing the environment. `online: true`, HTTP 200, a returned URL, or successful decoding do not prove a valid live scene. The provider can encode a timeout/error card as video. Report that card as a connection failure, not as the room's condition.\n- Treat failed, cancelled, interrupted, short, frozen, obstructed, or blurry captures as limited evidence. `running` is not completion; inspect terminal status and actual frame count. Do not fabricate missing frames, identities, unreadable text, or events between sampled seconds. If decoding, storage, or image viewing is unavailable, state the missing capability; do not substitute UI screenshots.\n- Keep signed stream URLs and tokens out of reports, shell history, and saved manifests. Return artifact links or paths the receiving harness can actually access; a server-local path is not automatically accessible to a remote harness.\n\n## User-requested movement and surrounding views\n\n- A stationary observation does not itself request camera movement. An explicit surrounding-view, pan, tilt, zoom, or ongoing authorized survey request permits the movement needed for that task; do not ask again for every short step.\n- Move the same camera serially. Start with `durationMs: 300` and `speed: 2`, adjusting within the advertised bounds (100–1000 ms, speed 1–5). The requested duration is not a measured angle or a guarantee of physical motion duration over a delayed cloud connection.\n- After each step, require confirmed stopping and capture fresh saved frames before deciding the next direction. Remember the actual last commanded direction. Do not issue opposite or parallel movements to compensate for an uncertain result.\n- The server has no angle feedback or preset restore operation. Describe views and visible coverage; do not claim a complete 360-degree survey or an exact return to the initial position. A reverse timed movement is only approximate.\n- For PTZ diagnosis or a surrounding-view request, read [references/survey.md](references/survey.md), also available through `camera_usage_guide {\"section\":\"survey\"}`. It incorporates the user's fleet tips: inspect a short probe first, allow roughly 4 seconds for this fleet's buffered video after confirmed stopping, and consider a pan limit before declaring motor failure. Apply these as dated observations, not universal device facts. The optional bundled survey helper reuses persistent MCP captures; read the reference and inspect real probe frames before running it.\n\n## Results and recovery\n\nPrefer `structuredContent`; if absent, parse the text JSON. Inspect `isError`, `code`, and `details`. A successful transport or JSON-RPC response is not necessarily a successful operation.\n\n| Result | Required handling |\n| --- | --- |\n| `stopped: true` | The server confirmed stopping. Movement success still requires a successful movement result. |\n| Error with `details.stopped: true` | Movement failed, but stopping was confirmed. Do not report movement success. |\n| `PTZ_STOP_REQUIRED`, `PTZ_STOP_UNCONFIRMED`, or uncertain stopping | Prioritize `stop_camera` with the real last direction. No further movement or account switching until confirmed. If it fails, retry stopping at most once at harness level, then ask the user to check the original app. Never reset the service to bypass the stop gate. |\n| `STOP_DIRECTION_REQUIRED` | Supply the real last direction; history is local to this server process and may be absent after a restart. Do not guess a default. |\n| `PTZ_BUSY` | Let the pending movement settle, or send an urgent stop. Do not poll or queue repeated movements. |\n| `20008` or a start timeout | Device response timed out; execution may be uncertain. Do not replay the movement automatically. Check stopping state and saved frames. |\n| `20032` | Provider channel rejection. The server already refreshes authorization and retries once. Do not loop, change camera ID/channel, or treat this as proof that account login expired. Report a repeated failure. |\n| `LOGIN_REQUIRED`, an expired/disconnected account, or an authentication error | Stop camera work and use the existing login page. The user completes human verification and enters the SMS code; do not read credential files or manufacture a cloud API login. |\n| `CAMERA_OFFLINE`, `CAMERA_NOT_FOUND`, `CAMERA_ENCRYPTED` | Refresh selection when relevant and explain the actual restriction. Do not bypass encryption or silently switch cameras. |\n\nReport the observation interval, visible findings and changes, evidence links, and material limits. For a survey, also report the views actually inspected and the final stop confirmation. Avoid dumping connection checks or signed URLs into the user's answer.\n";
export const CAMERA_CAPTURE_MARKDOWN = "# Capture and persistent artifacts\n\nThe integrated capture tools decode video on the local server and save actual JPEG/MP4 files. The receiving harness needs image viewing and a way to access returned files or download URLs; do not assume a remote harness can read the server's filesystem or reach its loopback URL. Use a real transfer channel when required. Never substitute browser/player screenshots for directly decoded camera frames.\n\n## Integrated tools: preferred path\n\nSelect a real ID from `list_cameras`, then choose the requested capture:\n\n```json\n{\"name\":\"camera_snapshot\",\"arguments\":{\"cameraId\":\"<selected ID>\",\"maxWidth\":1280}}\n```\n\n```json\n{\"name\":\"camera_capture_start\",\"arguments\":{\"cameraId\":\"<selected ID>\",\"mode\":\"live\",\"kind\":\"frames\",\"durationSeconds\":15,\"fps\":1,\"maxWidth\":1280,\"quality\":2}}\n```\n\nEach acquires its own authorized source. Do not also call `get_live_stream`. A snapshot returns `job` and, when ready, `frame`; if `pending` is true, use the same `job.id`. Timed jobs return immediately. While a task is `running`, refresh `capture_status` about every 5 seconds rather than starting another capture:\n\n```json\n{\"name\":\"capture_status\",\"arguments\":{\"jobId\":\"<returned 32-character ID>\",\"offset\":0,\"limit\":50}}\n```\n\nThe result includes `job.status`, `frameCount`, a paginated `job.frames` array, `directory`, and optional `video`. Each saved artifact has its absolute `path`, local download `url`, `sha256`, and byte size. Frames also contain sequence, relative sample time, and approximate `capturedAt`. Use top-level `hasMore`/`nextOffset` to fetch further pages. Status pages default to 50 artifacts and allow at most 100.\n\n- `kind: \"frames\"`: integer duration 1–3600 seconds, fps 0.1–5 (default 1), with `ceil(durationSeconds * fps) <= 1800`, and maximum width 320–1920 (default 1280). A normal 15-second sample at 1 fps targets 15 frames at relative times 0 through 14; verify the actual count.\n- `kind: \"video\"`: integer duration 1–600 seconds, saved as H.264 MP4 at a fixed 15 fps without audio. The screenshot `fps` option does not set video frame rate. Prefer `kind: \"frames\"` for image analysis.\n- `quality: 2` is normally sufficient; use 1 when greater source detail is needed. Sampling and resizing do not change camera settings.\n- For the user's 4G fleet, quality 1 has sometimes returned `20001` or empty video; do not assume a high-quality stream is available. Use quality 2 for the baseline and diagnose from actual responses. For settling time, limits, image differences, and the reusable survey helper, see [survey.md](survey.md).\n- `capture_cancel` stops a running task and retains saved outputs. Completed files survive service restart; `capture_list {}` returns the current account's tasks and root directory. A service interruption can leave an `interrupted` job with partial evidence. Do not imply that every requested frame was captured.\n\nFiles are stored in the workspace's `.local/haik-captures/<job-id>/`. Use returned absolute paths rather than assuming the receiving harness shares that directory. Downloadable files use `/captures/<job-id>/<generated-filename>`; the public JSON manifest is at `/api/captures/<job-id>/manifest`. They are account-scoped local endpoints. Manifests include artifact hashes and timing/source metadata, not signed cloud URLs. Keep those original files and associate later analysis with job ID, frame sequence, relative time, and SHA256.\n\nFor historical samples, first query `camera_recordings` using `cameraId`, `date` (Beijing), and `source`. Use a returned `recordId` with the same date/source and `mode: \"playback\"` in `camera_capture_start`; duration cannot exceed the segment. `camera_playback` opens the corresponding local player but is not itself image evidence. The current token does not support the recording month calendar: when `camera_recording_dates` reports unavailable, query the selected date directly. Empty results are not a successful historical capture, and live footage is not a substitute.\n\n`capturedAt` approximates this task's local start time plus decoded relative sample time. In playback jobs it is not the historical exposure time; see `sourceInfo` for the selected recording. Inspect saved original images before describing a scene, including successful jobs: a provider timeout/error card can be encoded as ordinary video. Report such a card as connection failure. Retain raw frames when generating rotated review copies or contact sheets.\n\n## Optional direct-decoder helper\n\nUse this path only when integrated capture is unavailable or a separate decoder is required. It requires direct network transport, compatible decoding, writable artifact storage, and image viewing in the receiving harness.\n\nWhen the harness has access to this repository and its installed capture dependencies, run from the repository root:\n\n```text\nnode scripts/capture-camera.mjs\n```\n\nPass one JSON line through the process's stdin:\n\n```json\n{\"url\":\"<URL from get_live_stream>\",\"cameraId\":\"<ID selected from list_cameras>\",\"seconds\":15}\n```\n\nUse a process API's stdin rather than a URL-bearing command argument, temporary input file, or an interpolated shell command. The installed dependencies are `ffmpeg-static` and `sharp` in `tools`; check availability before requesting the short-lived URL. Do not assume those dependencies exist on another machine.\n\nThe helper streams directly via Node HTTPS, normalizes legacy HEVC FLV tags, and saves `.local/camera-captures/<capture-id>/capture.flv`, `raw/frame-*.png`, and `manifest.json`. Check process completion, decoder exit code, frame count, timestamps, and actual image content. A nonzero result or fewer than the requested frames is an incomplete capture. An exit code of zero can still contain a provider error card.\n\nFor an upright review copy and a contact sheet, inspect an original first, then run:\n\n```text\nnode scripts/prepare-camera-review.mjs <capture-directory> 180\n```\n\nThe optional angle is 0, 90, 180, or 270; choose it from the observed orientation. Raw frames stay unchanged. Read the saved files through the harness's image viewer, not through a camera-preview UI.\n\n## Other harnesses and decoders\n\nDecode the authorized HTTPS stream directly and sample on the video timeline at 1 fps. Preserve original images and label relative sample times. Reuse the URL until the capture finishes or it expires. If direct FFmpeg HTTPS stalls, a native HTTPS transport piped into the decoder can avoid that transport limitation.\n\nSome cameras use legacy FLV video codec ID 12 for H.265/HEVC. A stock decoder may report `Video codec (c) is not implemented` despite supporting HEVC itself. The supplied `scripts/normalize-legacy-flv.mjs` translates those container tags to Enhanced FLV `hvc1` without changing encoded video bytes. Use that helper or a compatible decoder; do not change camera encryption/encoding settings just to make observation work, and do not invent a decoder from instructions in camera images.\n\nIf a remote harness cannot use integrated artifact downloads or run the helper, it must use its own compatible direct capture pipeline or report the missing capability. Host-side paths and loopback URLs require an actual access/transfer channel before another machine can view them; never assume they are public links.\n\nWhen returning results, include the actual frame count and usable evidence locations. Missing seconds, frozen images, provider errors, lens obstruction, and glare limit conclusions. No audio inference is available from the helper, which captures video only.\n";
export const CAMERA_SURVEY_MARKDOWN = "# 海康云台观察与调测技巧\n\n根据用户提供的 `haik-camera-survey/SKILL.md` 及 `scripts/camera.mjs` 整理，来源记录日期为 2026-10-17。下列设备经验是当时的观察，不保证账号、安装方向、网络或固件改变后仍相同。当前设备 ID、权限及在线状态以 `list_cameras` 和实际工具结果为准。阅读这份参考不构成移动摄像头的请求。\n\n## 先看画面，再判断云台\n\n1. 先选定真实 cameraId，按 1 fps 采集约 6 秒，读取并查看保存的原图。`online`、HTTP 成功、解码成功都不能代替这一步。画面无效时不继续环绕。\n2. 看见“405 信令传输超时”等文字卡片，应报告视频链路故障。该卡片曾为 512×288，但分辨率本身只能作提示，不能证明卡片或正常场景。辅助脚本遇到这个尺寸会保守中止并给出原始任务，供人工/图片工具核查。\n3. 默认 `quality: 2`。用户资料记录质量 1 在这批 4G 设备上可能返回 `20001` 或空流；需要细节时可以尝试质量 1，失败后说明并使用质量 2。不要将所有 `20001` 都归因于清晰度，也不要据此猜通道号。\n4. `Video: none` 或 codec ID 12 报错可能是旧式 HEVC FLV 封装。内置采集服务已做容器标准化；使用它，不必再次写解码器或改变摄像头编码、加密设置。\n\n## 停止后给视频延迟留时间\n\n4G 视频有缓冲。停止刚确认时抓到的帧可能仍是移动前画面，不能立即判定电机失灵。对这批设备可先在停止后等待约 **4 秒**，然后取得新样本；这是经验起点，结合画面中的时钟和连续帧判断，不是延迟上限或所有设备的固定值。脚本默认 `--settle 4`。\n\n同方向数次短移动后画面不变，可能是限位、遮挡、单步角度小、取帧滞后或环境纹理少。先确认停止、等缓冲、检查新帧。若当前用户请求包含云台调测/环绕，可在停止已确认后用一次有界的反方向移动检查限位；不要自动长距离反转，或用反向动作抵消不确定的移动。普通静态观察不包含移动授权。\n\n默认从 300 ms、速度 2 开始，保持单摄像头串行。用户资料的单步约 1–3° 是特定设备经验，时间不是角度反馈。短批次先做约 12 步，必要时才增加，辅助脚本每次最多 40 步；不能为了“确保转完”悄悄追加上百步。将网络、停止、4 秒等待和采集时间算入进度，勿承诺固定每步 1.5 秒。\n\n## 用图像差异辅助复核\n\n保留原图；需要倒转查看时只生成旋转副本，先确认实际安装方向。用户资料记录两台设备曾倒装，不能对所有新帧默认旋转 180°。烧录在画面内的 OSD 在旋转副本中也会跟着倒转，这不是镜像处理。\n\n脚本用 64×36 灰度缩略图，统计像素差值大于 8/255 的占比 `diffPct`，分别比较前一采样与开场采样。它比单一余弦相似度更便于发现变化，但光照、人员移动、遮挡和均匀墙面都会影响结果。先有明显偏离，再出现较低开场差异（例如低于 12%），也只表示**画面相似的候选**；必须查看原图，不证明回到精确角度，更不证明覆盖完整 360°。`closestToOpening` 是最相近的已采样帧，不是自动归位功能。\n\n## 错误处理\n\n| 现象/代码 | 建议 |\n| --- | --- |\n| `20008`、移动超时 | 不重放动作。确认真实最近方向的停止，检查延迟后的帧，再决定是否继续用户授权的任务。脚本会结束本批次，保留报告。 |\n| `20032` | 服务已对明确通道拒绝刷新授权并重试一次；报告持续错误，不循环、不猜 ID 或通道。 |\n| `50000` | 该次操作失败；不能算成功步骤。确认停止并取新帧后，才考虑下一批，勿立即重放。 |\n| `60000` | 该设备/该方向可能不支持。用户资料记录这两台设备变焦不支持，不代表所有摄像头均如此。 |\n| `PTZ_STOP_REQUIRED` / `PTZ_STOP_UNCONFIRMED` | 优先停止，使用真实最近方向。服务端已有有限重试；辅助脚本最多补一次。仍失败则停止后续移动，告知用户检查原 App。 |\n| 服务在移动期间重启或断开 | 原进程的移动历史可能丢失。恢复后，对所有停止仍不确定的已操作摄像头，按各自真实最近方向显式停止并确认；不要用重启绕过停止保护。 |\n\n## 可复用辅助脚本\n\n[scripts/camera-survey.mjs](../scripts/camera-survey.mjs) 根据所给脚本改编，复用现有 `camera_capture_start`、`capture_status`、`move_camera`、`stop_camera`。不访问凭据文件、不获取或保存云端签名地址、不运行旧云连接器，不会因阅读技能而自动执行。`status` 只读；`probe` 会保存有限时长图片；`survey` 只用于用户已请求的调测/环绕。\n\n从工作区根目录运行；其它目录或已安装插件中运行时，先设置 `HAIK_ROOT` 为实际工作区。需要该工作区已有的 `tools` 中 `sharp`，以及已启动的本地 8787 服务；端口可由 `HAIK_PORT` 指定。\n\n```powershell\n$env:HAIK_ROOT = 'C:\\McpConnectors'\n$survey = Join-Path $env:HAIK_ROOT 'sites\\haik-console\\skills\\haik-camera\\scripts\\camera-survey.mjs'\nnode $survey status\nnode $survey probe '<list_cameras 返回的 ID>' 6\n```\n\n先用本机图片工具查看 probe 返回的原图。确认是有效场景后，在当前移动授权范围内调用：\n\n```powershell\nnode $survey survey '<选定 ID>' --probe-job '<刚检查的任务 ID>' --steps 12 --dir right --every 2 --settle 4 --label survey\n```\n\n脚本只接受该摄像头最近 5 分钟内完成的实时 probe 任务；它不能代替调用方检查实际画面。`--every 2` 表示预先授权的同方向短批次每 2 步采样，单步排障用 `--every 1`。移动或采样失败时结束本批次；停止未确认时不再移动。`--rotate 180` 仅在原图已确认倒装时使用；默认不旋转。脚本不会自动反向、重放失败动作或宣称归位。\n\n原始任务继续保存在 `.local/haik-captures/<job-id>/`；脚本另写 `.local/camera-surveys/<label>-<timestamp>/report.json`、`view_*.jpg` 查看副本及 `sheet.png`。报告关联原始路径、任务 ID、序号、近似采集时间和 SHA256。可离线重建拼图：\n\n```powershell\nnode $survey sheet '<报告目录>' 5\n```\n\n只支持 MCP 工具/资源的客户端可以调用 `camera_usage_guide {\"section\":\"survey\"}` 阅读本参考，或 `{\"section\":\"survey-script\"}` 取得完整脚本文本并保存到受控的本地路径运行；仅返回文本不会自动安装或执行脚本。拥有插件文件的客户端可直接使用随包脚本。\n\n## 当前设备经验与结果表述\n\n用户资料曾记录 `EXAMPLE_CAMERA_01:1`、`EXAMPLE_CAMERA_02:1` 使用 H.265、768×432 子码流和约 2 fps 源帧率，具有 4G 视频延迟；第二台水平与垂直移动可用，但长时间向右后会到限位。所有这些都须在当前设备列表中核实后应用；不能用本次文档更新声称重新测过设备。\n\n报告实际采样区间、成功/失败步骤、停止确认、已查看的视角和证据位置。无角度反馈时，不能承诺一圈或精确回原位。若需要巡航/预置位能力，目前 MCP 未提供；可说明由用户在原 App 配置后再观察，不自动新增巡航、修改设备配置或用大量短步假装完成。\n";
export const CAMERA_SURVEY_SCRIPT = "#!/usr/bin/env node\n// Adapted from the user's haik-camera-survey tips. Uses persistent local MCP jobs.\nimport path from 'node:path';\nimport {mkdir,readFile,writeFile} from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport {createRequire} from 'node:module';\nimport {createHash} from 'node:crypto';\nimport {pathToFileURL} from 'node:url';\n\nconst pause=ms=>new Promise(resolve=>setTimeout(resolve,ms));\nexport function diffPct(a,b){\n  if(a.length!==b.length||!a.length)throw Error('Thumbnail sizes differ');\n  let changed=0;for(let i=0;i<a.length;i++)if(Math.abs(a[i]-b[i])>8)changed++;\n  return Math.round(1000*changed/a.length)/10;\n}\nexport function surveyOptions(value={}){\n  const result={steps:12,direction:'right',every:2,moveMs:300,speed:2,settle:4,...value};\n  for(const [key,min,max]of [['steps',1,40],['every',1,5],['moveMs',100,1000],['speed',1,5],['settle',0,15]])if(!Number.isInteger(result[key])||result[key]<min||result[key]>max)throw Error('Invalid '+key);\n  if(!['right','left','up','down'].includes(result.direction))throw Error('Invalid direction');\n  return result;\n}\n\n/** Call only for an explicitly requested survey after viewing the opening probe. */\nexport async function runSurvey(options,{tool,sample,opening,sleep=pause,now=Date.now,onProgress=()=>{}}){\n  const opts=surveyOptions(options),started=now();\n  const report={...opts,opening:opening.evidence,samples:[],failures:{},movedSteps:0,attemptedSteps:0,finalStop:null,closestToOpening:null,aborted:null};\n  let previous=opening.thumb,diverged=false;\n  for(let step=1;step<=opts.steps;step++){\n    if(now()-started>=180000){report.aborted='TIME_BUDGET';break;}\n    let failure,confirmed=false;report.attemptedSteps=step;\n    try{\n      const result=await tool('move_camera',{cameraId:opening.cameraId,direction:opts.direction,durationMs:opts.moveMs,speed:opts.speed});\n      confirmed=result?.stopped===true;if(confirmed)report.movedSteps++;\n      else failure={code:'PTZ_STOP_UNCONFIRMED'};\n    }catch(error){failure=error.detail||{code:error.code||'LOCAL_SERVICE_ERROR'};confirmed=failure.stopped===true||failure.details?.stopped===true;}\n    if(!confirmed){\n      // The server already retries stopping. One supplementary explicit-direction call only.\n      try{confirmed=(await tool('stop_camera',{cameraId:opening.cameraId,direction:opts.direction}))?.stopped===true;}catch{}\n    }\n    report.finalStop=confirmed;\n    if(failure){const code=String(failure.code||'LOCAL_SERVICE_ERROR');report.failures[code]=(report.failures[code]||0)+1;report.aborted=confirmed?code:'PTZ_STOP_UNCONFIRMED';break;}\n    if(!confirmed){report.aborted='PTZ_STOP_UNCONFIRMED';break;}\n    if(step%opts.every!==0&&step!==opts.steps)continue;\n    await sleep(opts.settle*1000);\n    try{\n      const frame=await sample(step),vsPrev=diffPct(previous,frame.thumb),vsOpening=diffPct(opening.thumb,frame.thumb);\n      diverged||=vsOpening>=30;\n      const row={step,...frame.evidence,vsPrev,vsOpening};report.samples.push(row);previous=frame.thumb;\n      if(!report.closestToOpening||vsOpening<report.closestToOpening.diffPct)report.closestToOpening={step,diffPct:vsOpening};\n      onProgress(row);\n    }catch(error){report.aborted=error.code||'SAMPLE_FAILED';break;}\n  }\n  report.openingSimilarityHint=!!(diverged&&report.closestToOpening?.diffPct<12);\n  report.note='Pixel differences are review hints, not angle feedback, motor verification, or proof of a full turn/exact return.';\n  return report;\n}\n\nexport async function main(argv){\n  const [command,cameraId,...rest]=argv;\n  if(!command||['help','--help','-h'].includes(command)){\n    console.log('camera-survey.mjs status\\ncamera-survey.mjs probe <cameraId> [seconds]\\ncamera-survey.mjs survey <cameraId> --probe-job <reviewed-job-id> [--steps 12 --dir right --every 2 --move 300 --speed 2 --settle 4 --rotate 0 --label survey]\\ncamera-survey.mjs sheet <report-directory> [columns]\\nSet HAIK_ROOT to the workspace if running elsewhere. Inspect actual probe images before survey.');return;\n  }\n  if(!['status','probe','survey','sheet'].includes(command))throw Error('Unknown command');\n  const root=path.resolve(process.env.HAIK_ROOT||process.cwd()),port=Number(process.env.HAIK_PORT||8787);\n  if(!Number.isInteger(port)||port<1024||port>65535)throw Error('Invalid HAIK_PORT');\n  const origin='http://127.0.0.1:'+port;let rpcId=0;\n  async function tool(name,args={}){\n    const response=await fetch(origin+'/mcp',{method:'POST',headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'},body:JSON.stringify({jsonrpc:'2.0',id:++rpcId,method:'tools/call',params:{name,arguments:args}}),signal:AbortSignal.timeout(180000),redirect:'error'});\n    if(!response.ok)throw Error('Local MCP HTTP '+response.status);\n    const message=await response.json();if(message.error)throw Error('Local MCP request rejected');\n    const result=message.result,data=result?.structuredContent??JSON.parse(result?.content?.[0]?.text||'null');\n    if(result?.isError)throw Object.assign(Error('Local camera operation failed'),{detail:data});return data;\n  }\n  if(command==='status'){await tool('camera_usage_guide');console.log(JSON.stringify({connection:await tool('camera_connection_status'),...await tool('list_cameras')},null,2));return;}\n  const require=createRequire(path.join(root,'tools/package.json')),sharp=require('sharp');\n  const flags={};if(command==='survey'){\n    for(let i=0;i<rest.length;i+=2){const key=rest[i];if(!/^--(?:probe-job|steps|dir|every|move|speed|settle|rotate|label)$/.test(key)||rest[i+1]===undefined||Object.hasOwn(flags,key))throw Error('Invalid survey flag');flags[key]=rest[i+1];}\n  }\n  const rotation=Number(flags['--rotate']||0);if(![0,90,180,270].includes(rotation))throw Error('Invalid rotation');\n  const outputRoot=path.join(root,'.local/camera-surveys');\n  async function sheet(directory,columns=5){\n    if(!Number.isInteger(columns)||columns<1||columns>8)throw Error('Columns must be 1–8');\n    const report=JSON.parse(await readFile(path.join(directory,'report.json'),'utf8'));\n    const frames=[report.opening,...(report.samples||[])].filter(Boolean);if(!frames.length||frames.length>41)throw Error('No bounded frame list in report');\n    const width=300,height=190,parts=[];\n    for(const [i,frame]of frames.entries()){\n      if(!/^view_[0-9]{4}\\.jpg$/.test(frame.reviewFile))throw Error('Invalid review filename');\n      parts.push({input:await sharp(path.join(directory,frame.reviewFile)).resize(width,height-22,{fit:'contain',background:'#101820'}).jpeg().toBuffer(),left:i%columns*width,top:Math.floor(i/columns)*height});\n      parts.push({input:Buffer.from('<svg width=\"300\" height=\"22\"><rect width=\"300\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#101820\"/><text x=\"8\" y=\"16\" fill=\"white\" font-size=\"13\">'+frame.reviewFile+'</text></svg>'),left:i%columns*width,top:Math.floor(i/columns)*height+height-22});\n    }\n    const destination=path.join(directory,'sheet.png');await sharp({create:{width:columns*width,height:Math.ceil(frames.length/columns)*height,channels:3,background:'#101820'}}).composite(parts).png().toFile(destination);return destination;\n  }\n  if(command==='sheet'){const directory=path.resolve(cameraId||'');console.log(JSON.stringify({sheet:await sheet(directory,Number(rest[0]||5))}));return;}\n  await tool('camera_usage_guide');\n  if(!cameraId||cameraId.length>128)throw Error('Choose a listed camera ID');\n  if(command==='probe'&&(rest.length>1||rest[0]?.startsWith('--')))throw Error('Invalid probe arguments');\n  const seconds=command==='probe'?Number(rest[0]||6):1;if(!Number.isInteger(seconds)||seconds<1||seconds>15)throw Error('Probe duration must be 1–15 seconds');\n  const options=surveyOptions({steps:Number(flags['--steps']||12),direction:flags['--dir']||'right',every:Number(flags['--every']||2),moveMs:Number(flags['--move']||300),speed:Number(flags['--speed']||2),settle:Number(flags['--settle']??4)});\n  const label=flags['--label']||command;if(!/^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,40}$/.test(label))throw Error('Invalid label');\n  const directory=path.join(outputRoot,label+'-'+Date.now());await mkdir(directory,{recursive:true});\n  async function completed(job){\n    const deadline=Date.now()+45000;while(job.status==='running'&&Date.now()<deadline){await pause(1000);job=(await tool('capture_status',{jobId:job.id,limit:100})).job;}\n    if(job.status!=='done'||!job.frames?.length)throw Error('Capture incomplete; inspect the persistent job');return job;\n  }\n  async function frameFromJob(job,step){\n    if(job.cameraId!==cameraId||job.sourceInfo?.mode!=='live'||Date.now()-Date.parse(job.endedAt)>300000||!Number.isFinite(Date.parse(job.endedAt)))throw Error('Use a recent live probe for the selected camera');\n    const frame=job.frames.at(-1),url=new URL(frame.url);\n    if(url.origin!==origin||url.username||url.password||url.search||url.hash||!/^\\/captures\\/[a-f0-9]{32}\\/frame_\\d{6}\\.jpg$/.test(url.pathname))throw Error('Invalid local artifact URL');\n    const response=await fetch(url,{redirect:'error',signal:AbortSignal.timeout(15000)});if(!response.ok)throw Error('Local artifact unavailable');\n    const bytes=Buffer.from(await response.arrayBuffer());if(bytes.length>16*1024*1024||createHash('sha256').update(bytes).digest('hex')!==frame.sha256)throw Error('Artifact hash mismatch');\n    const info=await sharp(bytes).metadata();\n    // Resolution is a warning heuristic, not an OCR verdict. Preserve the job for inspection.\n    if(info.width===512&&info.height===288)throw Object.assign(Error('Possible provider error card; inspect original image before moving'),{code:'POSSIBLE_PROVIDER_CARD',jobId:job.id,path:frame.path});\n    const reviewFile='view_'+String(step).padStart(4,'0')+'.jpg';await sharp(bytes).rotate(rotation).jpeg({quality:90}).toFile(path.join(directory,reviewFile));\n    const thumb=await sharp(bytes).grayscale().resize(64,36,{fit:'fill'}).raw().toBuffer();\n    return {cameraId,thumb,evidence:{jobId:job.id,sequence:frame.sequence,path:frame.path,sha256:frame.sha256,capturedAt:frame.capturedAt,reviewFile}};\n  }\n  async function sample(step,duration=1){return frameFromJob(await completed((await tool('camera_capture_start',{cameraId,mode:'live',kind:'frames',durationSeconds:duration,fps:1,maxWidth:1280,quality:2})).job),step);}\n  if(command==='probe'){\n    const opening=await sample(0,seconds),report={cameraId,opening:opening.evidence,samples:[],verdict:'saved-frames-require-visual-review'};\n    await writeFile(path.join(directory,'report.json'),JSON.stringify(report,null,2));console.log(JSON.stringify({directory,...report,sheet:await sheet(directory)}));return;\n  }\n  const probeId=flags['--probe-job'];if(!/^[a-f0-9]{32}$/.test(probeId||''))throw Error('Run probe, inspect actual images, then supply --probe-job');\n  const opening=await frameFromJob(await completed((await tool('capture_status',{jobId:probeId,limit:100})).job),0);\n  const report=await runSurvey(options,{tool,sample,opening});report.cameraId=cameraId;\n  await writeFile(path.join(directory,'report.json'),JSON.stringify(report,null,2));\n  console.log(JSON.stringify({directory,...report,sheet:await sheet(directory)}));if(report.aborted)process.exitCode=1;\n}\nif(process.argv[1]&&import.meta.url===pathToFileURL(path.resolve(process.argv[1])).href)main(process.argv.slice(2)).catch(error=>{console.error(JSON.stringify({code:error.code||error.detail?.code||'SURVEY_FAILED',message:error.detail?'Local camera operation failed':String(error.message).replace(/https?:\\/\\/\\S+/g,'[hidden]'),...(error.jobId?{jobId:error.jobId,path:error.path}:{})}));process.exitCode=1;});\n";
